 "description": "Recently, the rate at which consumers abandon their online shopping carts has been gradually rising to more than 70 percent in 2026, showing a higher difficulty for e-commerce sites to convert website traffic into purchases. In 2024, food and beverage was one of the product categories with the lowestonline cart abandonment rate, confirming the sector\u2019s relatively high conversion rate. In the United States, the primary reason why customers abandoned their shopping carts is that extra costs such as shipping, tax, and service fees were too high at checkout."
